# ==== T-FMT-B — an interior comment inside a GROUPED IMPORT stays inside it.
# SCOPE CLAIM: the comment-placement cell only, for `import a.{X, Y}`. The
# author-ORDER cells live in `import_author_order.gg`.
#
# This was a FILED DEFECT: the grouped import was the single declared
# `Gate::UngatedCarveOut` from the interior-comment gate, and the comment
# escaped the group and re-emerged at COLUMN 0 documenting the next item.
# Removing the name sort (canon call 6, 2026-08-16) removed the carve-out's
# whole reason — emitted order is now source order, so the forward-only comment
# cursor can interleave per element — and the group routes through
# `emit_delimited_list` like every other list. The gate then keeps the comment
# with the name below it, and the list stays exploded because it carries one.
#
# Pre-fix RED (measured): the whole group packed to
# `import std.math.{abs, sqrt}` and `# SEN import-group` came back at column 0,
# above `int main():`.
#
# ⚠ The inline spelling `{sqrt, # c, abs}` does NOT parse — a line comment
# swallows the rest of the line — so the multi-line form is the only repro.
import std.math.{
    sqrt,
    # SEN import-group
    abs,
}

int main():
    print(1)
    return 0
